WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.680
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:10.380
Reading this paper was an absolute&nbsp;
delight, but also a shocking experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.460
I will try to tell you why and you can&nbsp;
let me know if you feel like that too.&nbsp;

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:21.120
This is Microsoft’s assessment of the&nbsp;
capabilities of OpenAI’s GPT-4 AI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:27.660
and I am out of words. This&nbsp;
is unbelievable. Why? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:33.420
let’s see together. By the end of this&nbsp;
video, I think you will be out of words too.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:40.380
Let’s start immediately with what I find to&nbsp;
be perhaps the most fun experiment. Scientists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:47.580
had the idea to play a text-based game with&nbsp;
GPT-4 where the AI can navigate through a map,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:53.700
and we make up a little adventure and&nbsp;
tell it what happened. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:01.140
it starts in the main room, and it chooses to&nbsp;
move left. We say that this is now kitchen 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:09.780
so it says that it wishes to move up. And so on&nbsp;
it goes. Nothing too crazy here. Right? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:15.060
check this out. After reaching the goal,&nbsp;
it can build up and reconstruct the map&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:22.260
of the whole game. But wait, how do we know?&nbsp;
This is just a bunch of text. This one, yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:29.880
but don’t forget, this is an assistant, so&nbsp;
we can ask it to, and get this, draw a map.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:36.960
And the map it has drawn it perfect! And the funny&nbsp;
thing is that no one even asked it to remember the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:44.460
layout because it will be asked about later.&nbsp;
I absolutely loved this. This is so much fun.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:52.680
Now, remember, this can only answer in terms of&nbsp;
text, however, we can create images by using text.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:59.820
One example of this is called TikZ, which can&nbsp;
create beautiful images from a text description,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:05.760
but you can ask almost anyone who has ever&nbsp;
used it, have them describe the experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:12.900
and “joy” is not likely a word you will hear&nbsp;
from them. If only we had an AI that could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:19.020
do all this for us. You know what? Let’s&nbsp;
try it! Let’s ask it to write the code for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:26.160
a little person built from the letters of the&nbsp;
alphabet. This is not bad, but we can ask for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:33.660
some improvements. Yes, and then, add some&nbsp;
shirt and pants, and there we go! Great job.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:40.680
Or, we can also ask for a unicorn as well. And&nbsp;
here we find something super interesting. Hold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:47.700
on to your papers Fellow Scholars, because it&nbsp;
improves over time. These prompts were run in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.980
the span of a month, and over time,&nbsp;
the system became better and better.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:59.220
What’s more, it can even create a really&nbsp;
simple mockup of a video game. And now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:05.580
we can give this to another AI, Stable&nbsp;
Diffusion to embellish it a little. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.560
there we go. That almost looks like&nbsp;
a screenshot from a real video game.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:16.140
And while looking through the results,&nbsp;
we forgot that a miracle happened. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:22.260
is the miracle? Well, this version of&nbsp;
the GPT-4 AI has never seen an image.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:29.940
This is an AI that reads text. It has&nbsp;
never ever seen an image in its life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:36.240
Yet, it learned to see, sort of, just from&nbsp;
the textual descriptions of things it had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.960
read on the internet.
That is insane.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:48.840
Let’s test that some more! Have a look at this.&nbsp;
Little AI, imagine that we have a book, 9 eggs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:56.820
a laptop, a bottle and a nail. Please tell me&nbsp;
how to stack them onto each other in a stable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:02.580
manner. Now, the previous version was&nbsp;
off to a great start, and then it said.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:10.440
“Place the eggs on top of the nail, making&nbsp;
sure they are balanced and not tilting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:16.680
one side.” You know what, little AI? You do&nbsp;
it. I will believe this when I see it. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:23.700
let’s see the new one. It says: “Arrange the&nbsp;
9 eggs in a 3 by 3 square on top of the book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:28.740
leaving some space between them.&nbsp;
The eggs will form a second layer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:34.320
and distribute the weight evenly. Make&nbsp;
sure the eggs are not cracked or broken,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:40.740
and handle them gently to avoid dropping them.”&nbsp;
Now that’s what I am talking about! Checkmark!

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:47.100
And there is so much more to talk about, I&nbsp;
don’t even know where to start. When asked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.240
it can even create a simple little&nbsp;
video game in HTML and Javascript,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:58.560
even with rudimentary physics. Its coding skills&nbsp;
are so sharp, it would likely be hired as a real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:04.620
software engineer. And that is perhaps an&nbsp;
understatement. Look, I loved this part:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:12.720
Time allotted: 2 hours. Time spent:&nbsp;
1 second shy of 4 minutes. Not hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:20.100
Minutes. Holy mother of papers. It crushed&nbsp;
the interview faster than any human would.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:25.500
I was also shocked by its mathematical&nbsp;
skills. It can be given these problems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.420
from the International Mathematics&nbsp;
Olympiad, these folks love creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:36.720
problems that look like a piece of cake, but&nbsp;
require considerable mathematical experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:44.040
and thought to solve well. But this comes&nbsp;
out almost instantly. And it nailed it.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:51.000
In a different, physics-inspired problem from&nbsp;
somewhere else, the previous version of it just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:57.780
made something up. Not cool. So, can the new&nbsp;
one solve it? Well, it identified that using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:04.380
integral calculus is necessary, what’s more,&nbsp;
like a good student, it starts integrating by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:12.420
part. That is fantastic. And the result is that&nbsp;
it almost nailed it. It made an arithmetic error,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:18.840
but other than that, it did very well. That is&nbsp;
the perfect metaphor of the whimsical nature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:25.200
of the AI systems we have today. They understand&nbsp;
how to apply integration by parts in reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:31.920
which is outstanding, and then, it slips&nbsp;
up when it needs to count up a few objects.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:40.200
So, conclusions. Where does all this put us?&nbsp;
Get this - Microsoft claims that GPT-4 might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:46.860
have a spark of general intelligence. This is&nbsp;
something that most people thought, and perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:54.780
still think is not possible at all, but even if&nbsp;
it is, surely not in our lifetime. And here we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.780 --> 00:07:01.980
are. The future is here. This is intelligence like&nbsp;
we’ve never seen before. What a time to be alive!

